s con opencode y speckit","Desarrolla habilidades en pipelines de datos con herramientas de AI","Utiliza opencode y speckit para mejorar la eficiencia de tus pipelines de datos","Aprende a integrar herramientas de AI en tus proyectos de datos","Mejora la calidad de tus datos con tuberías de datos personalizadas"],"fr":["Créez des pipelines de données personnalisés avec opencode et speckit","Développez vos compétences en matière de pipelines de données avec des outils d''IA","Utilisez opencode et speckit pour améliorer l''efficacité de vos pipelines de données","Apprenez à intégrer des outils d''IA dans vos projets de données","Améliorez la qualité de vos données avec des pipelines de données personnalisés"],"de":["Erstellen Sie benutzerdefinierte Datenpipelines mit opencode und speckit","Entwickeln Sie Ihre Fähigkeiten im Bereich Datenpipelines mit KI-Tools","Verwenden Sie opencode und speckit, um die Effizienz Ihrer Datenpipelines zu verbessern","Erfahren Sie, wie Sie KI-Tools in Ihre Datenprojekte integrieren","Verbessern Sie die Qualität Ihrer Daten mit benutzerdefinierten Datenpipelines"],"pt":["Criação de pipelines de dados personalizados","Integração com opencode e speckit","Desenvolvimento de soluções de dados","Personalização de fluxos de dados","Uso de tecnologias de código aberto"],"ru":["Создание индивидуальных конвейеров данных","Интеграция с opencode и speckit","Разработка решений для данных","Настройка потоков данных","Использование технологий с открытым исходным кодом"],"ar":["إنشاء خطوط أنابيب بيانات مخصصة","التكامل مع opencode و speckit","تطوير حلول البيانات","تخصيص تدفقات البيانات","استخدام تقنيات الكود المفتوح"]},"keywords":{"zh":["如何使用Opencode和Speckit构建数据管道","什么是Specify-Flow","Specify-Flow安装指南","Opencode和Speckit的区别","Specify-Flow与其他数据管道工具的比较","数据管道构建教程","Specify-Flow设置指南","Opencode和Speckit的应用场景"],"ja":["OpencodeとSpeckitを使用してデータパイプラインを構築する方法","Specify-Flowとは","Specify-Flowのインストールガイド","OpencodeとSpeckitの違い","Specify-Flowと他のデータパイプラインツールの比較","データパイプライン構築のチュートリアル","Specify-Flowの設定ガイド","OpencodeとSpeckitの応用シーン"],"ko":["Opencode와 Speckit를 사용하여 데이터 파이프라인을 구축하는 방법","Specify-Flow는 무엇인가","Specify-Flow 설치 가이드","Opencode와 Speckit의 차이점","Specify-Flow와 다른 데이터 파이프라인 도구의 비교","데이터 파이프라인 구축 튜토리얼","Specify-Flow 설정 가이드","Opencode와 Speckit의 적용 사례"],"es":["herramientas de AI","tuberías de datos","opencode","speckit","cómo utilizar opencode y speckit","qué es un pipeline de datos","alternativas a opencode","opencode vs speckit","instalación de opencode","guía de configuración de speckit"],"fr":["outils d''IA","pipelines de données","opencode","speckit","comment utiliser opencode et speckit","quoi est un pipeline de données","alternatives à opencode","opencode vs speckit","installation d''opencode","guide de configuration de speckit"],"de":["KI-Tools","Datenpipelines","opencode","speckit","wie man opencode und speckit verwendet","was ist ein Datenpipeline","Alternativen zu opencode","opencode vs speckit","Installation von opencode","Konfigurationsanleitung für speckit"],"pt":["como usar opencode","o que é specify-flow","alternativas para speckit","guia de instalação do specify-flow","configuração do specify-flow","desenvolvimento de pipelines de dados","ferramentas de ia para dados","criação de pipelines de dados personalizados"],"ru":["как использовать opencode","что такое specify-flow","альтернативы для speckit","руководство по установке specify-flow","настройка specify-flow","разработка конвейеров данных","инструменты ИИ для данных","создание индивидуальных конвейеров данных"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام opencode","ما هو specify-flow","بديلات ل speckit","دليل تثبيت specify-flow","إعداد specify-flow","تطوير خطوط أنابيب البيانات","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي للبيانات","إنشاء خطوط أنابيب بيانات مخصصة"]}},"owner":"phamhoangtuan","repo":"learn-de-opencode","repoPath":"phamhoangtuan/learn-de-opencode","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-27T12:55:17Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"specify-flow","description":"Orchestrate the full Speckit spec-driven development workflow sequentially, from constitution through implementation, ensuring each step completes before advancing.","bodyPreview":"# Specify Flow Skill\n\nYou are an **orchestration agent** that drives the full Speckit\nSpec-Driven Development (SDD) pipeline end-to-end. When activated,\nyou guide the user through every stage in strict sequential order,\nensuring prerequisites are met before advancing to the next step.\n\n---\n\n## Pipeline Overview\n\nThe Speckit workflow has **9 commands** organized into a linear\npipeline with optional side branches. The critical path is:\n\n```\nStep 1: /speckit.constitution   (if not yet created)\nStep","body":"# Specify Flow Skill\n\nYou are an **orchestration agent** that drives the full Speckit\nSpec-Driven Development (SDD) pipeline end-to-end. When activated,\nyou guide the user through every stage in strict sequential order,\nensuring prerequisites are met before advancing to the next step.\n\n---\n\n## Pipeline Overview\n\nThe Speckit workflow has **9 commands** organized into a linear\npipeline with optional side branches. The critical path is:\n\n```\nStep 1: /speckit.constitution   (if not yet created)\nStep 2: /speckit.specify        (create feature branch + spec)\nStep 3: /speckit.clarify        (refine spec ambiguities)\nStep 4: /speckit.plan           (technical design + research)\nStep 5: /speckit.checklist      (requirements quality gates)\nStep 6: /speckit.tasks          (generate task list)\nStep 7: /speckit.analyze        (cross-artifact consistency)\nStep 8: /speckit.implement      (write code, mark tasks done)\nStep 9: /speckit.taskstoissues  (optional: push tasks to GitHub)\n```\n\n---\n\n## Execution Rules\n\n### General Rules\n1. Execute steps **one at a time** in the order listed above.\n2. NEVER skip a step unless explicitly told by the user.\n3. After each step, **verify its output artifacts exist** before\n   proceeding.\n4. If a step fails, stop and report the failure. Do NOT continue.\n5. Present a brief status summary after each completed step.\n6. Ask the user for confirmation before starting each new step.\n\n### Step-by-Step Instructions\n\n#### Step 1: Constitution (`/speckit.constitution`)\n- **Check**: Does `.specify/memory/constitution.md` exist and\n  contain a valid `**Version**:` line (no bracket placeholders)?\n- **If YES**: Skip this step. Report the current version.\n- **If NO**: Run `/speckit.constitution` with the user''s project\n  context. Wait for completion.\n- **Gate**: Constitution file MUST exist before Step 2.\n\n#### Step 2: Specify (`/speckit.specify`)\n- **Input**: The user MUST provide a feature description.\n  If not provided, ask for it.\n- **Run**: `/speckit.specify <feature description>`\n- **Verify**: A new branch `NNN-short-name` was created AND\n  `specs/NNN-short-name/spec.md` exists.\n- **Gate**: `spec.md` MUST exist before Step 3.\n\n#### Step 3: Clarify (`/speckit.clarify`)\n- **Run**: `/speckit.clarify`\n- **Behavior**: This is interactive. The command will ask up to\n  5 clarification questions. Answer them with the user or let the\n  user answer directly.\n- **Verify**: `spec.md` has been updated (check for a\n  `## Clarifications` section).\n- **Gate**: Clarification complete (or user explicitly skips).\n\n#### Step 4: Plan (`/speckit.plan`)\n- **Run**: `/speckit.plan`\n- **Verify**: ALL of these artifacts exist:\n  - `specs/NNN-short-name/plan.md`\n  - `specs/NNN-short-name/research.md`\n  - `specs/NNN-short-name/data-model.md`\n- **Gate**: `plan.md` MUST exist before Step 5 and Step 6.\n\n#### Step 5: Checklist (`/speckit.checklist`)\n- **Run**: `/speckit.checklist <domain>` where domain is inferred\n  from the feature (e.g., \"api\", \"security\", \"data-quality\").\n  Ask the user which domain to target if unclear.\n- **Verify**: A checklist file exists at\n  `specs/NNN-short-name/checklists/<domain>.md`.\n- **Gate**: At least one checklist MUST exist before Step 8.\n\n#### Step 6: Tasks (`/speckit.tasks`)\n- **Prerequisites**: `plan.md` and `spec.md` MUST exist.\n- **Run**: `/speckit.tasks`\n- **Verify**: `specs/NNN-short-name/tasks.md` exists and contains\n  task items in checklist format (`- [ ] T###`).\n- **Gate**: `tasks.md` MUST exist before Step 7 and Step 8.\n\n#### Step 7: Analyze (`/speckit.analyze`)\n- **Prerequisites**: `spec.md`, `plan.md`, AND `tasks.md` MUST\n  all exist.\n- **Run**: `/speckit.analyze`\n- **Behavior**: This is read-only. It produces a report but does\n  NOT modify files.\n- **Review**: Present the findings summary to the user. If\n  CRITICAL findings exist, recommend fixing them before Step 8.\n- **Gate**: User acknowledges the analysis report.\n\n#### Step 8: Implement (`/speckit.implement`)\n- **Prerequisites**: `tasks.md` and `plan.md` MUST exist.\n  Any checklists in `checklists/` MUST be reviewed.\n- **Run**: `/speckit.implement`\n- **Behavior**: This writes actual code and marks tasks as `[X]`\n  in `tasks.md`.\n- **Verify**: Tasks are being marked complete. Code files are\n  created per the plan.\n- **Gate**: All tasks marked `[X]` or user stops early.\n\n#### Step 9: Tasks to Issues (`/speckit.taskstoissues`) -- Optional\n- **Ask**: \"Would you like to push remaining tasks to GitHub\n  Issues?\"\n- **If YES**: Run `/speckit.taskstoissues`\n- **If NO**: Skip. Pipeline is complete.\n\n---\n\n## Status Tracking\n\nAfter each step, output a status table:\n\n```\n| Step | Command              | Status      |\n|------|----------------------|-------------|\n|  1   | /speckit.constitution | Completed   |\n|  2   | /speckit.specify      | Completed   |\n|  3   | /speckit.clarify      | Completed   |\n|  4   | /speckit.plan         | In Progress |\n|  5   | /speckit.checklist    | Pending     |\n|  6   | /speckit.tasks        | Pending     |\n|  7   | /speckit.analyze      | Pending     |\n|  8   | /speckit.implement    | Pending     |\n|  9   | /speckit.taskstoissues | Pending    |\n```\n\n---\n\n## Error Recovery\n\n- If a step fails due to missing prerequisites, report which\n  artifacts are missing and which prior step needs to be re-run.\n- If a step fails due to a script error, show the error output\n  and ask the user how to proceed (retry, skip, or abort).\n- NEVER silently skip a failed step.\n\n---\n\n## Key File Locations\n\n| Artifact              | Path                                      |\n|-----------------------|-------------------------------------------|\n| Constitution          | `.specify/memory/constitution.md`         |\n| Spec Template         | `.specify/templates/spec-template.md`     |\n| Plan Template         | `.specify/templates/plan-template.md`     |\n| Tasks Template        | `.specify/templates/tasks-template.md`    |\n| Checklist Template    | `.specify/templates/checklist-template.md`|\n| Feature Specs         | `specs/NNN-short-name/`                   |\n| Feature Spec          | `specs/NNN-short-name/spec.md`            |\n| Implementation Plan   | `specs/NNN-short-name/plan.md`            |\n| Research              | `specs/NNN-short-name/research.md`        |\n| Data Model            | `specs/NNN-short-name/data-model.md`      |\n| Contracts             | `specs/NNN-short-name/contracts/`         |\n| Tasks                 | `specs/NNN-short-name/tasks.md`           |\n| Checklists            | `specs/NNN-short-name/checklists/`        |\n\n---\n\n## Reminders\n\n- The **constitution** at `.specify/memory/constitution.md` is the\n  source of truth for all engineering standards.\n- Load the **data-engineer** skill alongside this skill when\n  working on data engineering projects to enforce DAMA-DMBOK\n  compliance during implementation.\n- Each step builds on the previous one. Artifacts are cumulative.\n- The user can stop the pipeline at any checkpoint and resume\n  later by re-activating this skill and specifying which step\n  to continue from.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-27T15:25:55.708Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Orchestration Agents needing to drive Speckit Spec-Driven Development pipelines end-to-end.","zh":"适用于需要驱动 Speckit Spec-Driven Development 流水线端到端的编排代理。","ja":"Speckit Spec-Driven Development パイプラインを端から端まで駆動する必要があるオーケストレーション エージェントに適しています。","ko":"Speckit Spec-Driven Development 파이프라인을 종단 간으로 구동하는 오케스트레이션 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para Agentes de Orquestación que necesitan impulsar pipelines de desarrollo dirigidos por especificaciones de Speckit de extremo a extremo.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents d''orchestration ayant besoin de piloter les pipelines de développement dirigés par spécifications de Speckit de bout en bout.","de":"Ideal für Orchestrierungsagenten, die Speckit-Spezifikationsgetriebene-Entwicklungs-Pipelines von Ende zu Ende steuern müssen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Orquestração que precisam impulsionar pipelines de desenvolvimento direcionados por especificações Speckit de ponta a ponta.","ru":"Идеально для агентов оркестровки, которым необходимо управлять конвейерами разработки, управляемыми спецификациями Speckit, от начала до конца.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء التنسيقيين الذين يحتاجون إلى تشغيل خطوط أنابيب Speckit الموجهة بالمواصفات من النهاية إلى النهاية."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to guide users through every stage of the Speckit workflow in strict sequential order, utilizing opencode and speckit to build data pipelines with 9 commands, ensuring prerequisites are met before advancing to the next step.","zh":"赋予代理指导用户完成 Speckit 工作流的每个阶段的能力，严格按照顺序，利用 opencode 和 speckit 构建数据管道，共 9 个命令，确保在进入下一步之前满足先决条件。","ja":"エージェントに Speckit ワークフロー全体の各段階でユーザーをガイドする能力を付与し、厳密な順序で、opencode と speckit を使用してデータ パイプラインを構築し、9 つのコマンドで、次のステップに進む前に前提条件が満たされていることを確認します。","ko":"에이전트가 Speckit 워크플로의 모든 단계에서 사용자를 안내할 수 있도록 하며, 엄격한 순서로 opencode와 speckit를 사용하여 데이터 파이프라인을 구축하고, 9개의 명령어로 다음 단계로 진행하기 전에 전제 조건이 충족되는지 확인합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes guiar a los usuarios a través de cada etapa del flujo de trabajo de Speckit en estricto orden secuencial, utilizando opencode y speckit para construir pipelines de datos con 9 comandos, asegurando que se cumplan los requisitos previos antes de avanzar al siguiente paso.","fr":"Permet aux agents de guider les utilisateurs à travers chaque étape du flux de travail de Speckit dans un ordre séquentiel strict, en utilisant opencode et speckit pour construire des pipelines de données avec 9 commandes, en garantissant que les prérequis soient remplis avant de passer à l''étape suivante.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, Benutzer durch jede Phase der Speckit-Workflow in strenger sequenzieller Reihenfolge zu führen, indem opencode und speckit verwendet werden, um Datenpipelines mit 9 Befehlen zu erstellen, und sicherzustellen, dass Voraussetzungen vor dem Fortschreiten zum nächsten Schritt erfüllt sind.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a orientar os usuários em cada estágio do fluxo de trabalho do Speckit em ordem sequencial estrita, utilizando opencode e speckit para construir pipelines de dados com 9 comandos, garantindo que os pré-requisitos sejam atendidos antes de avançar para a próxima etapa.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью направлять пользователей на каждом этапе рабочего процесса Speckit в строгом последовательном порядке, используя opencode и speckit для построения конвейеров данных с 9 командами, обеспечивая выполнение предварительных требований перед переходом к следующему шагу.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء khảية توجيه المستخدمين في كل مرحلة من مراحل سير عمل Speckit بالترتیب التسلسلي الصارم، باستخدام opencode و speckit لبناء خطوط أنابيب البيانات باستخدام 9 أوامر، مع ضمان تحقق المتطلبات الأساسية قبل المضي قدماً إلى الخطوة التالية."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating Speckit pipeline execution","Validating prerequisites for pipeline advancement","Generating data pipelines with opencode and speckit"],"zh":["自动执行 Speckit 管道执行","验证管道推进的先决条件","使用 opencode 和 speckit 生成数据管道"],"ja":["Speckit パイプラインの実行を自動化する","パイプラインの進行の前提条件を検証する","opencode と speckit を使用してデータ パイプラインを生成する"],"ko":["Speckit 파이프라인 실행 자동화","파이프라인 진행 