t Technologien wie React und Node.js","Kompatibilität mit CLI","Detaillierte Dokumentation für Entwickler"],"pt":["Coleção de jogos para crianças","Opções de entretenimento para crianças","Fácil de usar e navegar","Compatível com diferentes plataformas","Atualizações regulares de novos jogos"],"ru":["Коллекция игр для детей","Варианты развлечения для детей","Легко использовать и навигировать","Совместимо с разными платформами","Регулярные обновления новых игр"],"ar":["مجموعة من ألعاب الأطفال","خيارات لتسلية الأطفال","سهلة الاستخدام والتنقل","متوافقة مع منصات مختلفة","تحديثات دورية لألعاب جديدة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["如何使用petstore-checklist","什么是AI智能工具","petstore-checklist替代品","petstore-checklist vs 其他工具","petstore-checklist安装","petstore-checklist设置指南","AI游戏开发","游戏集合创建工具"],"ja":["petstore-checklistの使い方","AIエージェントとは","petstore-checklistの代替","petstore-checklist vs 他のツール","petstore-checklistのインストール","petstore-checklistの設定ガイド","AIゲーム開発","ゲーム集の作成ツール"],"ko":["petstore-checklist 사용 방법","AI 에이전트란","petstore-checklist 대안","petstore-checklist vs 다른 도구","petstore-checklist 설치","petstore-checklist 설정 가이드","AI 게임 개발","게임 모음 생성 도구"],"es":["herramientas AI para desarrolladores","colección de juegos para niños","cómo utilizar petstore-checklist","petstore-checklist vs otras herramientas AI","instalación de petstore-checklist","guía de configuración de petstore-checklist","desarrollo de juegos con petstore-checklist","usos de petstore-checklist en la industria del juego"],"fr":["outils IA pour les développeurs","collection de jeux pour enfants","comment utiliser petstore-checklist","petstore-checklist vs d''autres outils IA","installation de petstore-checklist","guide de configuration de petstore-checklist","développement de jeux avec petstore-checklist","utilisations de petstore-checklist dans l''industrie du jeu"],"de":["KI-Tools für Entwickler","Sammlung von Spielen für Kinder","wie man petstore-checklist verwendet","petstore-checklist vs andere KI-Tools","Installation von petstore-checklist","Konfigurationsanleitung für petstore-checklist","Spielentwicklung mit petstore-checklist","Anwendungen von petstore-checklist in der Spieleindustrie"],"pt":["como usar o agente de petstore","o que é agente de petstore","agente de petstore alternativa","agente de petstore vs outros","instalar agente de petstore","guia de configuração do agente de petstore","jogos para crianças","entretenimento para crianças"],"ru":["как использовать ИИ Агент для Petstore","что такое ИИ Агент для Petstore","ИИ Агент для Petstore альтернатива","ИИ Агент для Petstore vs другие","установить ИИ Агент для Petstore","руководство по настройке ИИ Агента для Petstore","игры для детей","развлечения для детей"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام أداة قائمة مراجعة لمتجر الحيوانات الأليفة","ما هي أداة قائمة مراجعة لمتجر الحيوانات الأليفة","أداة قائمة مراجعة لمتجر الحيوانات الأليفة بديلة","أداة قائمة مراجعة لمتجر الحيوانات الأليفة مقابل أخرى","تثبيت أداة قائمة مراجعة لمتجر الحيوانات الأليفة","دليل إعداد أداة قائمة مراجعة لمتجر الحيوانات الأليفة","ألعاب للأطفال","تسلية للأطفال"]}},"owner":"a1flecke","repo":"games-for-my-kids","repoPath":"a1flecke/games-for-my-kids","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-01T23:51:36Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"petstore-checklist","description":"Pre-implementation checklist for lizzies-petstore sessions. Prints the coding rules most likely to cause bugs. Run this before writing any session code.","bodyPreview":"Read the session file, then confirm each rule below before writing code.\n\n## Spec Code Has Bugs — Fix Before Implementing\n\nSession specs often contain code samples that violate CLAUDE.md rules. Before using any code sample from the spec, scan it for these patterns and replace them:\n\n| Spec pattern | Fix |\n|---|---|\n| `style.display = ''none''` / `''block''` / `''flex''` | Use a CSS class instead (`.active`, `.open`, `.hidden`) |\n| `onclick=\"...\"` HTML attribute | Remove attr; bind with `addEventListen","body":"Read the session file, then confirm each rule below before writing code.\n\n## Spec Code Has Bugs — Fix Before Implementing\n\nSession specs often contain code samples that violate CLAUDE.md rules. Before using any code sample from the spec, scan it for these patterns and replace them:\n\n| Spec pattern | Fix |\n|---|---|\n| `style.display = ''none''` / `''block''` / `''flex''` | Use a CSS class instead (`.active`, `.open`, `.hidden`) |\n| `onclick=\"...\"` HTML attribute | Remove attr; bind with `addEventListener` in JS |\n| `.onclick = () => ...` | Use `addEventListener` — no stacking risk |\n| `.sort(() => Math.random() - 0.5)` | Fisher-Yates (see Shuffling section) |\n| `color: #636e72` | `color: var(--text-secondary)` |\n| `localStorage.getItem / .setItem` | `SaveManager.load()` / `SaveManager.save()` with key `lizzies-petstore-save` |\n| `window.x = window.x \\|\\| new X()` | `window.x = new X()` in `game.init()` — always fresh |\n| `new AudioContext()` in constructor | Create lazily on first `_getCtx()` call; `ctx.resume().then(() => schedule())` |\n| Independent `requestAnimationFrame` in a manager | Only `game.js` owns the RAF loop — expose `update(dt)` and `draw(ctx, w, h)` |\n| `touchstart` / `touchmove` / `touchend` | Use Pointer Events: `pointerdown` / `pointermove` / `pointerup` |\n| `Math.random()` in cached texture generation | Use seeded PRNG (`_seededRandom(hash)`) so re-cache produces identical results |\n| `globalAlpha < 1` then `source-atop` compositing | Draw fully opaque first, apply covering/pattern, then reduce alpha in a separate step |\n| `escHtml()` on `setAttribute(''aria-label'', ...)` | Don''t escape — `setAttribute` doesn''t parse HTML entities; `&amp;` reads literally to AT |\n| `timer % interval < threshold` on float timer | Use interval counter: `if (timer >= nextTime) { nextTime += interval; }` |\n| `aria-pressed` on `role=\"option\"` elements | Use `aria-selected` — `aria-pressed` is for toggle buttons, not listbox options |\n| `role=\"listitem\"` on `<button>` elements | Remove — `role=\"listitem\"` overrides implicit button role, breaking AT |\n| `aria-live` + `aria-hidden` on same element | Remove `aria-live`; `role=\"status\"` implies it. Toggling `aria-hidden` on a live region causes phantom AT announcements |\n| `SaveManager.load()`/`getCreature()` per frame | Cache on state entry: `this._cachedCreature = saveManager.getCreature(id)` |\n| LRU/indexOf/splice in draw loop | Only update LRU on build/invalidate, never in draw/update (hot path) |\n| Static background redrawn per frame | Cache to offscreen canvas on init/resize; `drawImage()` per frame |\n| `ctx.save()`/`ctx.restore()` per particle | Batch: set `globalAlpha` directly per particle, reset once at end |\n\n---\n\n## Canvas Performance Rules\n\n### Offscreen Caching (CreatureCache)\n- Each body part rendered once to its own offscreen canvas at display size × DPR\n- `invalidatePart(slot)` re-renders only the changed part — never re-cache all parts\n- Game loop composites via `drawImage()` — a single GPU-accelerated call per part\n- Covering textures pre-rendered as separate texture canvases — one-time cost\n- Max **30 offscreen canvases** active — LRU evict if exceeded\n\n### No DOM During Gameplay\n- All gameplay rendering on Canvas — no `createElement`, `innerHTML`, `classList` during the RAF loop\n- DOM overlays (needs meters, buttons) updated only on value change, not every frame\n\n### RAF Delta Time\n- Always `requestAnimationFrame` with delta time for movement/animation\n- Cap delta at **50ms** for iPad Safari RAF throttling\n- Never use `setInterval` for the game loop\n\n---\n\n## Timer Lifecycle Pattern\n\nEvery manager with `setTimeout`/`setInterval` must follow this pattern exactly:\n\n```js\nclass SomeManager {\n    constructor() {\n        this._mainTimer = null;\n        this.onComplete = null;\n    }\n    cancel() {\n        clearTimeout(this._mainTimer); this._mainTimer = null;\n        this.onComplete = null;\n    }\n    complete() {\n        const cb = this.onComplete;\n        this.cancel();\n        if (cb) cb();\n    }\n    start(...) { this.cancel(); /* init */ }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Touch Input Rules\n\n- **Pointer Events** only (`pointerdown/move/up`) — never touch events\n- CSS `touch-action: none` on canvas\n- `setPointerCapture()` for drag tracking\n- Coordinate conversion: `(clientX - rect.left) * (canvas.width / rect.width)`\n- **60px minimum hitboxes** for body parts in creator\n- **50px snap radius** for attachment points\n\n---\n\n## Web Audio API (iOS Safari)\n\n- `AudioContext` created lazily on first user gesture — never in constructor\n- `ctx.resume().then(() => schedule())` — oscillators inside `.then()`\n- Sine waves only + low-pass filter for creature voices\n- `speechSynthesis.cancel()` + 50ms delay before `speak()` if used\n\n---\n\n## Screen Visibility\n\n- **Screens** → `.active` class\n- **Overlays** (settings, wardrobe panel) → `.open` class\n- **Internal toggles** → `.hidden` class\n- Never `style.display` in JS\n\n---\n\n## Modal Dialogs\n\n- `role=\"dialog\"`, `aria-modal=\"true\"`, `aria-label=\"...\"`\n- First focusable element = close button\n- Focus trap: Tab/Shift-Tab cycles within overlay\n- Escape to close (with `.contains(''open'')` guard)\n- On close: return focus to trigger element\n- `aria-hidden` always explicit `''true''`/`''false''` — never `removeAttribute`\n\n---\n\n## State Machine\n\n```\nTITLE → CREATOR → BIRTH_ANIMATION → CARE (hub) → PARK\n                                   ↕ WARDROBE\n                                   ↕ ROOM_EDIT\n  GALLERY ↔ CARE\n  GALLERY → CREATOR (edit existing)\n```\n\n- State transitions cancel all active timers/animations\n- Confirmation dialog when leaving CREATOR with unsaved changes\n- Document for each new state: entry/exit states, game loop behavior, input handling\n\n---\n\n## Single RAF Chain — game.js Owns the Loop\n\nOnly `game.js` may call `requestAnimationFrame`. Every other class exposes:\n- `update(dt)` — advance state\n- `draw(ctx, w, h)` — render to canvas\n\n---\n\n## Z-Order Render Constant\n\n```js\nconst RENDER_ORDER = [''legs'', ''tail'', ''torso'', ''wings'', ''head'', ''eyes'', ''extras'', ''accessories''];\n```\n\n---\n\n## Animation: Pivot-Based\n\n- Each part has a pivot point + simple curves (sine rotation, bounce, scale)\n- `ctx.save()` / `ctx.restore()` must bracket every transform\n- Delta-time based, cap at 50ms\n\n---\n\n## Save System\n\n- **One key**: `lizzies-petstore-save` — always through SaveManager\n- Schema versioned: `schemaVersion: 1`\n- Auto-save debounced 2s\n- Backup every 5th save to `lizzies-petstore-save-backup`\n- `_defaults()` must include ALL keys read by game.js\n- Quota error → user-visible toast\n\n---\n\n## Needs Decay\n\n- Decay ONLY during active play (1pt / 2min / need)\n- Floor at **20** — never desperate\n- No real-time decay when app closed\n- On reopen: creature greets happily regardless of absence\n- Max decay capped at 24 hours\n\n---\n\n## Hot-Path Performance (60fps Draw/Update Loop)\n\nThe `_update(dt)` and `_draw()` functions run 60×/sec. Never do expensive or allocating work inside them:\n\n- **No `SaveManager.load()` or `getCreature()` per frame** — cache the creature ref on state entry\n- **No LRU tracking in draw calls** — only update on `buildCache()` / `invalidatePart()`\n- **Cache static backgrounds** (grid dots, gradients) to offscreen canvas — `drawImage()` per frame\n- **No per-particle `ctx.save()`/`ctx.restore()`** — set `globalAlpha` directly, reset once at end\n- **No `document.createElement()`** — all DOM creation in setup code\n\n---\n\n## Seeded PRNG for Cached Textures\n\nAny procedurally generated texture cached to an offscreen canvas must use a seeded PRNG (not `Math.random()`). Otherwise LRU eviction + re-cache produces different visuals.\n\nSeed from a hash of partId + color for deterministic results.\n\n---\n\n## source-atop Compositing Requires Opaque Base\n\nWhen using `globalCompositeOperation = ''source-atop''`, the base shape must be fully opaque. Semi-transparent base pixels cause `base_alpha × texture_alpha` blending — visually wrong.\n\nIf you need translucent final result: draw opaque → apply covering/pattern → composite the result at reduced alpha in a separate step.\n\n---\n\n## Periodic Effects: Interval Counters Not Modulus\n\n`timer % 100 < 20` on a float is unreliable. Use an explicit next-time counter:\n```js\nif (this._timer >= this._nextSparkleTime) {\n    this._nextSparkleTime = this._timer + 100;\n    spawnSparkle();\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Shuffling\n\nNever `.sort(() => Math.random() - 0.5)`. Fisher-Yates:\n```js\nfor (let i = arr.length - 1; i > 0; i--) {\n    const j = Math.floor(Math.random() * (i + 1));\n    [arr[i], arr[j]] = [arr[j], arr[i]];\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## WCAG Non-Negotiables\n\n- Never `user-scalable=no` in viewport meta\n- Touch targets >= 44px (60px for Creator palette)\n- Font: OpenDyslexic via CDN `<link>`, Comic Sans MS fallback\n- Min font size: 16px, line height 1.5×\n- Background: cream `#F5F0E8`, text: `#2C2416`, secondary: `#595143`\n- WCAG AA 4.5:1 — never `#666`, `#888`, `#999` on cream\n- No flashing/strobing\n- `ctx.font` always includes fallback: `''16px OpenDyslexic, \"Comic Sans MS\", cursive''`\n\n---\n\n## CSS ID Specificity\n\nNever put `display:` in a base ID rule:\n```css\n/* BAD */\n#screen-title { display: flex; }\n/* GOOD */\n#screen-title.active { display: flex; }\n```\n\n---\n\n## Session Spec Validation\n\nBefore implementing:\n1. Scan spec code samples against the pattern table above\n2. Confirm canvas rendering ownership is stated (game.js calls render, not manager)\n3. New state machine states must document transitions\n4. Default settings must have a rationale\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-02T03:56:00.710Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Web Development Agents needing to debug and optimize HTML and CSS code for pet store applications","zh":"非常适合需要调试和优化宠物商店应用程序HTML和CSS代码的Web开发智能体","ja":"ペットストアアプリケーションのHTMLおよびCSSコードのデバッグと最適化を必要とするWeb開発エージェントに最適です","ko":"애견숍 애플리케이션을 위한 HTML 및 CSS 코드 디버깅과 최적화가 필요한 웹 개발 에이전트에 완벽하게 적합합니다","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Desarrollo Web que necesitan depurar y optimizar código HTML y CSS para aplicaciones de tiendas de mascotas","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents de Développement Web ayant besoin de déboguer et d''optimiser le code HTML et CSS pour les applications d''animalerie","de":"Perfekt für Webentwicklungs-Agents, die HTML- und CSS-Code für Tierhandlung-Anwendungen debuggen und optimieren müssen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento Web que precisam depurar e otimizar código HTML e CSS para aplicações de pet store","ru":"Идеально подходит для веб-агентов разработки, которым требуется отладка и оптимизация HTML и CSS кода для приложений зоомагазинов","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء تطوير الويب الذين يحتاجون إلى تصحيح وتحسين كود HTML و CSS لتطبيقات متجر الحيوانات الأليفة"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to scan code samples for patterns that violate CLAUDE.md rules, replacing them with best practices such as using CSS classes instead of inline styles and binding events with addEventListener, ensuring compatibility with modern web standards and libraries like p5.js","zh":"使智能体能够扫描代码样本以查找违反CLAUDE.md规则的模式，并用最佳实践替换它们，例如使用CSS类而不是内联样式以及使用addEventListener绑定事件，确保与现代Web标准及p5.js等库的兼容性","ja":"CLAUDE.mdルールに違反するパターンのコードサンプルをスキャンし、インラインスタイルの代わりにCSSクラスを使用する、addEventListenerでイベントをバインドするなどのベストプラクティスに置き換えることで、p5.jsなどの最新のWeb標準やライブラリとの互換性を確保します","ko":"에이전트가 CLAUDE.md 규칙을 위반하는 패턴에 대한 코드 샘플을 스캔하여 인라인 스타일 대신 CSS 클래스 사용, addEventListener로 이벤트 바인딩과 같은 최적의 방법으로 대체함으로써 p5.js와 같은 현대적인 웹 표준 및 라이브러리와의 호환성을 보장합니다","es":"Permite a los agentes escanear muestras de código en busca de patrones que violen las reglas de CLAUDE.md, reemplazándolos con mejores prácticas como usar clases CSS en lugar de estilos en línea y vincular eventos con addEventListener, garantizando compatibilidad con estándares web modernos y bibliotecas como p5.js","fr":"Permet aux agents de scanner des échantillons de code pour détecter les modèles qui violent les règles CLAUDE.md, en les remplaçant par des bonnes pratiques telles que l''utilisation de classes CSS au lieu des styles en ligne et la liaison d''événements avec addEventListener, garantissant ainsi la compatibilité avec les standards web modernes et les bibliothèques comme p5.js","de":"Ermöglicht es Agents, Codebeispiele auf Muster zu scannen, die gegen CLAUDE.md-Regeln verstoßen, und ersetzt diese durch Best Practices wie die Verwendung von CSS-Klassen anstelle von Inline-Styles und das Binden von Ereignissen mit addEventListener, wodurch die Kompatibilität mit modernen Webstandards und Bibliotheken wie p5.js gewährleistet wird","pt":"Capacita os agentes a escanear amostras de código em busca de padrões que violem as regras do CLAUDE.md, substituindo-os por melhores práticas, como usar classes CSS em vez de estilos inline e vincular eventos com addEventListener, garantindo compatibilidade com padrões web modernos e bibliotecas como p5.js","ru":"Позволяет агентам сканировать образцы кода на наличие шаблонов, нарушающих правила CLAUDE.md, заменяя их лучшими практиками, такими как использование классов CSS вместо встроенных стилей и привязка событий с помощью addEventListener, обеспечивая совместимость с современными веб-стандартами и библиотеками, такими как p5.js","ar":"يمكن الوكلاء من فحص عينات الكود للبحث عن أنماط تنتهك قواعد CLAUDE.md، واستبدالها بأفضل الممارسات مثل استخدام فئات CSS بدلاً من الأنماط المضمنة وربط الأحداث باستخدام addEventListener، مما يضمن التوافق مع معايير الويب الحديثة والمكتبات مثل p5.js"},"useCases":{"en":["Debugging spec code for CLAUDE.md compliance","Generating CSS classes for dynamic styling","Validating HTML event bindings for security"],"zh":["调试规范代码以确保符合CLAUDE.md要求","为动态样式生成CSS类","验证HTML事件绑定以确保安全性"],"ja":["CLAUDE.md準拠のための仕様コードのデバッグ","動的スタイリングのためのCSSクラスの生成","セキュリティのためのHTMLイベントバインディングの検証"],"ko":["CLAUDE.md 준수를 위한 사양 코드 디버깅","