os CLI","en":"asciinema-demos"},"description":{"zh":"asciinema-demos是一款用于管理AI代理的命令行接口，提供便捷的开发体验","ja":"asciinema-demosはAIエージェントを管理するためのCLIで、開発者にとって便利なツールです","ko":"asciinema-demos는 AI 에이전트를 관리하는 명령줄 인터페이스로서 개발자에게 편리한 도구를 제공합니다","es":"Asciinema-demos es una CLI para gestionar agentes, ideal para desarrolladores que necesitan una herramienta de línea de comandos para administrar sus agentes...","fr":"Asciinema-demos est une CLI pour gérer les agents, idéale pour les développeurs qui ont besoin d''un outil de ligne de commande pour administrer leurs agents ...","de":"Asciinema-demos ist eine CLI für die Verwaltung von Agenten, ideal für Entwickler, die ein Kommandozeilen-Tool benötigen, um ihre Agenten effizient zu verwal...","pt":"O asciinema-demos CLI é uma ferramenta de linha de comando para gerenciar agentes, permitindo que os desenvolvedores trabalhem de forma eficiente","ru":"ИИ Агенты asciinema-demos CLI - это инструмент командной строки для управления агентами, позволяющий разработчикам работать эффективно","ar":"أداة asciinema-demos CLI هي أداة سطر أوامر لإدارة الوكلاء، مما يسمح للمطورين بالعمل بفعالية","en":"CLI for managing agents"},"definition":{"en":"CLI for managing agents"},"features":{"zh":["支持多种AI代理管理","提供便捷的命令行接口","提高开发效率","支持自定义配置","兼容多种开发环境"],"ja":["複数のAIエージェントを管理する","便利なCLIを提供する","開発の効率を上げる","カスタム設定をサポートする","複数の開発環境に対応する"],"ko":["다중 AI 에이전트 관리 지원","편리한 명령줄 인터페이스 제공","개발 효율성 향상","사용자 정의 설정 지원","다중 개발 환경 지원"],"es":["CLI para gestionar agentes","Integración con herramientas de desarrollo","Soporte para múltiples plataformas","Administración de agentes de forma eficiente","Compatibilidad con React, Python y Node.js"],"fr":["CLI pour gérer les agents","Intégration avec les outils de développement","Prise en charge de plusieurs plateformes","Administration des agents de manière efficace","Compatibilité avec React, Python et Node.js"],"de":["CLI für die Verwaltung von Agenten","Integration mit Entwicklungstools","Unterstützung für mehrere Plattformen","Verwaltung von Agenten in effizienter Weise","Kompatibilität mit React, Python und Node.js"],"pt":["Gerenciamento de agentes via linha de comando","Integração com ferramentas de desenvolvimento","Suporte a múltiplos agentes","Interface de usuário intuitiva","Documentação completa"],"ru":["Управление агентами через командную строку","Интеграция с инструментами разработки","Поддержка нескольких агентов","Интуитивно понятный интерфейс пользователя","Полная документация"],"ar":["إدارة الوكلاء عبر سطر الأوامر","التكامل مع أدوات التطوير","دعم عدة وكلاء","واجهة مستخدم بديهية","توثيق كامل"]},"keywords":{"zh":["如何使用asciinema-demos","什么是AI工具","asciinema-demos替代品","asciinema-demos vs 其他工具","asciinema-demos安装指南","asciinema-demos设置教程","AI代理管理","命令行接口","开发效率"],"ja":["asciinema-demosの使い方","AIエージェントとは","asciinema-demosの代替","asciinema-demos vs 他のツール","asciinema-demosのインストール方法","asciinema-demosの設定ガイド","AIエージェントの管理","CLI","開発の効率"],"ko":["asciinema-demos 사용법","AI 에이전트란","asciinema-demos 대안","asciinema-demos vs 다른 도구","asciinema-demos 설치 가이드","asciinema-demos 설정 튜토리얼","AI 에이전트 관리","명령줄 인터페이스","개발 효율성"],"es":["cómo usar asciinema-demos","qué es asciinema-demos","alternativa a asciinema-demos","asciinema-demos vs otras herramientas","instalación de asciinema-demos","guía de configuración de asciinema-demos","herramientas de AI para desarrolladores"],"fr":["comment utiliser asciinema-demos","qu''est-ce que asciinema-demos","alternative à asciinema-demos","asciinema-demos vs d''autres outils","installation d''asciinema-demos","guide de configuration d''asciinema-demos","outils d''IA pour les développeurs"],"de":["wie man asciinema-demos verwendet","was ist asciinema-demos","Alternative zu asciinema-demos","asciinema-demos im Vergleich zu anderen Tools","Installation von asciinema-demos","Konfigurationsanleitung für asciinema-demos","KI-Tools für Entwickler"],"pt":["como usar asciinema-demos","o que é asciinema-demos","alternativas para asciinema-demos","asciinema-demos vs outras ferramentas","instalar asciinema-demos","guia de configuração do asciinema-demos","ferramentas de AI para desenvolvedores","gerenciamento de agentes de IA"],"ru":["как использовать asciinema-demos","что такое asciinema-demos","альтернативы asciinema-demos","asciinema-demos vs другие инструменты","установить asciinema-demos","руководство по настройке asciinema-demos","инструменты ИИ для разработчиков","управление агентами ИИ"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام asciinema-demos","ما هو asciinema-demos","بديلات ل asciinema-demos","asciinema-demos مقابل أدوات أخرى","تثبيت asciinema-demos","دليل إعداد asciinema-demos","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي للمطورين","إدارة وكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي"]}},"owner":"imbue-ai","repo":"mng","repoPath":"imbue-ai/mng","stars":11,"forks":2,"updatedAt":"2026-03-04T00:30:16Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"asciinema-demos","description":"Create 1-3 short asciinema demo recordings (5-20 seconds each) that demonstrate completed work. Use only when explicitly instructed to create demos.","bodyPreview":"# Creating Asciinema Demos\n\nThis skill provides guidelines for creating short, looping terminal demo recordings that visually demonstrate completed work. The demos serve as proof that a task was done correctly and help reviewers quickly understand what changed.\n\n## Overview\n\nEach demo session produces 1-3 recordings (each 5-20 seconds) as looping GIFs. The workflow is:\n\n1. Plan what to demo\n2. Write demo and cleanup scripts\n3. Record with asciinema\n4. Verify the recordings\n5. Iterate if needed\n6","body":"# Creating Asciinema Demos\n\nThis skill provides guidelines for creating short, looping terminal demo recordings that visually demonstrate completed work. The demos serve as proof that a task was done correctly and help reviewers quickly understand what changed.\n\n## Overview\n\nEach demo session produces 1-3 recordings (each 5-20 seconds) as looping GIFs. The workflow is:\n\n1. Plan what to demo\n2. Write demo and cleanup scripts\n3. Record with asciinema\n4. Verify the recordings\n5. Iterate if needed\n6. Convert to GIF and (optionally) upload to a PR\n\n## Prerequisites\n\nThe following tools must be available:\n\n- `asciinema` (terminal recorder) -- records .cast files\n- `agg` (asciinema gif generator) -- converts .cast to .gif\n- `python3` with `json` module (standard library) -- for .cast file verification\n\nIf they are not, simply make a note in the PR that the demos could not be generated, and which tools should be installed to enable them.\n\n## Step 1: Plan the Demos\n\nBefore recording anything, think carefully about what to demo. This is the most important step.\n\n**Ask yourself:**\n\n- What are the 1-3 most important things to show?\n- What would convince a reviewer that the task was completed correctly?\n- What is the shortest path to showing each thing?\n- How can I ensure that all resulting demo resources are always safely cleaned up by the demo script after each execution?\n\n**Common demo types:**\n\n| Scenario | What to show |\n|---|---|\n| New CLI command | Run the command with typical arguments, show the output |\n| Bug fix | Show the fixed behavior |\n| Data/config change | Show the data exists and has correct values (e.g., `cat`, `jq`, `grep`) and that the core dependent behavior works |\n| Performance improvement | Run a benchmark or timed command showing the improvement (and the necessary context to understand) |\n| New feature in existing command | Run the command exercising the new feature |\n| Refactor (no behavior change) | Show that the core dependent behavior(s) still work |\n\n**Guidelines:**\n\n- Each demo should be 5-20 seconds. Shorter is better.\n- Focus on the output that matters -- don''t show lengthy setup or irrelevant output.\n- If demonstrating data, use commands like `cat`, `head`, `jq`, `grep`, or `sqlite3` to show the relevant parts.\n- If the change is not directly visible in the CLI (e.g., internal refactor), demo the tests passing or show downstream effects.\n\n## Step 2: Write Demo and Cleanup Scripts\n\nFor each demo, create a bash script for that specific demo. Place them in a temporary location or in `.demos/scripts/`.\n\n**Template for a demo script:**\n\n```bash\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Demo: Brief description of what this demonstrates\n\n# Optionally set up a clean prompt for the recording\nexport PS1=''$ ''\n\n# Add brief pauses between commands so the viewer can read the output\necho \"$ some-command --flag\"\nsome-command --flag\nsleep 1\n\necho \"\"\necho \"$ another-command\"\nanother-command\nsleep 1\n```\n\n**Important considerations for demo scripts:**\n\n### Handling commands that block or require input\n\nFor commands that would normally block waiting for input or run indefinitely:\n\n- Use `timeout` to limit execution time: `timeout 5 some-long-command`\n- Pipe input for interactive commands: `echo \"y\" | some-command`\n- Use `yes | head -1 |` for yes/no prompts\n- For commands that start background processes, run them and immediately show the result:\n  ```bash\n  some-command --background\n  sleep 2\n  show-status-command\n  ```\n\n### Simulating typed commands\n\nTo make the demo look natural (as if someone is typing), you can echo the command before running it:\n\n```bash\n# Show the command being \"typed\", then run it\necho ''$ mng list''\nmng list\nsleep 1\n```\n\nOr, for a more polished look, use a helper function that simulates typing:\n\n```bash\ntype_cmd() {\n    local cmd=\"$1\"\n    printf ''$ ''\n    for ((i=0; i<${#cmd}; i++)); do\n        printf ''%s'' \"${cmd:$i:1}\"\n        sleep 0.03\n    done\n    printf ''\\n''\n    eval \"$cmd\"\n}\n\ntype_cmd \"mng list\"\nsleep 1\n```\n\n### Keeping output clean\n\n- Set `export PS1=''$ ''` for a clean prompt\n- Redirect stderr if it would clutter the output: `command 2>/dev/null`\n- Use `head -n 20` or similar to truncate long output\n- Clear the screen between demos if needed: `clear`\n\n**Important considerations for cleanup scripts:**\n\n- The cleanup script *MUST* be run after running the demo\n- Be *very* careful with `rm` or any destructive commands! Always double-check that the script cannot accidentally delete important files or directories.\n- Name cleanup scripts like this: .demos/scripts/demo1_cleanup.sh\n\n## Step 3: Record\n\nUse the helper script `scripts/record_demo.sh` to record each demo:\n\n```bash\n./scripts/record_demo.sh <demo_script> <output_name> [options]\n```\n\n**Examples:**\n\n```bash\n# Basic recording\n./scripts/record_demo.sh .demos/scripts/demo1.sh feature-demo; .demos/scripts/demo1_cleanup.sh\n\n# Custom terminal size and speed\n./scripts/record_demo.sh .demos/scripts/demo1.sh feature-demo --cols 120 --rows 24 --speed 1.5; .demos/scripts/demo1_cleanup.sh\n\n# Recording without GIF conversion (for faster iteration)\n./scripts/record_demo.sh .demos/scripts/demo1.sh feature-demo --no-gif; .demos/scripts/demo1_cleanup.sh\n```\n\nThe script produces three files in `.demos/` (or the directory specified by `--out-dir`):\n\n- `<name>.cast` -- the asciinema recording\n- `<name>.gif` -- the GIF (unless `--no-gif`)\n- `<name>.txt` -- plain text dump of the recording output\n\n**Key options:**\n\n| Option | Default | Description |\n|---|---|---|\n| `--cols N` | 100 | Terminal width |\n| `--rows N` | 30 | Terminal height |\n| `--theme THEME` | monokai | GIF color theme |\n| `--font-size N` | 16 | Font size in pixels for GIF |\n| `--speed N` | 1 | Playback speed multiplier |\n| `--idle-limit N` | 2 | Max idle time between events (seconds) |\n| `--last-frame N` | 3 | How long the final frame displays (seconds) |\n| `--out-dir DIR` | .demos | Output directory |\n| `--no-gif` | | Skip GIF conversion (faster for iteration) |\n| `--no-loop` | | Disable GIF looping |\n\n## Step 4: Verify\n\nThis is critical. Since you cannot watch the GIF, you must verify the recording by reading the text dump.\n\n**Read the `.txt` file** to confirm:\n\n1. The expected commands appear in the output\n2. The expected output/results are visible\n3. There are no error messages or unexpected output\n4. The flow makes sense (commands appear in the right order)\n\n```bash\ncat .demos/feature-demo.txt\n```\n\nYou can also inspect the `.cast` file directly to check timing:\n\n```bash\n# Check the total duration (time of last event)\ntail -1 .demos/feature-demo.cast\n\n# Check all events\ncat .demos/feature-demo.cast\n```\n\n**Verification checklist:**\n\n- [ ] All expected commands are present in the output\n- [ ] All expected results/data are visible\n- [ ] No error messages or tracebacks\n- [ ] Recording duration is 5-20 seconds (check the timestamp of the last event in the .cast file)\n- [ ] Terminal size is appropriate for the content (no wrapping/truncation issues)\n\n## Step 5: Iterate\n\nIf the recording does not look right:\n\n1. Identify the problem from the `.txt` dump\n2. Fix the demo script\n3. Re-record (use `--no-gif` while iterating for speed)\n4. Verify again\n5. Once satisfied, do a final recording with GIF conversion\n\nCommon problems and fixes:\n\n| Problem | Fix |\n|---|---|\n| Output is truncated/wrapped | Increase `--cols` |\n| Recording is too long | Remove unnecessary `sleep` calls, use `--speed 2` |\n| Recording is too short | Add `sleep` calls between commands |\n| Command produced an error | Fix the demo script or the underlying issue |\n| Too much output | Use `head`, `tail`, or `grep` to filter |\n| Interactive command blocked | Use `timeout`, pipe input, or mock the interaction |\n\n## Step 6: Upload to PR\n\nIf the demos should be attached to a GitHub PR, you need to make the GIF accessible via URL.\n\n**NEVER try to commit files the demo files, especially not the GIFs**.\n\n**Instead, upload via GitHub''s attachment API**\n\nGitHub allows uploading images by posting them as assets. This avoids committing binary files to the repo. Use `gh` to create a release asset or attach to an issue/PR comment via the API.\n\n## Tips\n\n- **Start with `--no-gif`** while iterating on the demo script. Only convert to GIF once you are satisfied with the `.txt` output.\n- **Keep demos focused.** One concept per demo. If you need to show multiple things, make multiple short demos rather than one long one.\n- **Use `--speed 1.5` or `--speed 2`** if the demo has natural pauses that would make it feel slow.\n- **For data verification demos**, use colorized output when possible (e.g., `jq` with colors, `grep --color`). This makes the GIF more readable.\n- **Always run the cleanup script** after recording to ensure no leftover state could affect future runs or the user''s environment.\n- **Output directory**: The default `.demos/` directory is gitignored. **NEVER commit GIFs!**\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-04T01:54:50.072Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for CLI Agents needing to create interactive terminal demo recordings with asciinema","zh":"非常适合需要使用asciinema创建交互式终端演示录像的CLI代理","ja":"CLIエージェントがasciinemaを使用してインタラクティブなターミナルデモレコーディングを作成する必要がある場合に最適","ko":"asciinema를 사용하여 상호 작용형 터미널 데모 녹화를 생성해야 하는 CLI 에이전트에 적합","es":"Perfecto para agentes de CLI que necesitan crear grabaciones de demostración interactivas de terminal con asciinema","fr":"Parfait pour les agents CLI ayant besoin de créer des enregistrements de démonstration interactifs de terminal avec asciinema","de":"Perfekt für CLI-Agents, die interaktive Terminal-Demo-Aufnahmen mit asciinema erstellen müssen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes CLI que precisam criar gravações de demonstração interativa de terminal com asciinema","ru":"Идеально для агентов CLI, которым необходимо создавать интерактивные записи демонстрации терминала с помощью asciinema","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء CLI الذين يحتاجون إلى إنشاء تسجيلات демонстрация تفاعلية لمحطة الطرفية مع asciinema"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to generate looping GIFs using asciinema, providing visual proof of completed tasks and facilitating quick review with demo and cleanup scripts, all managed through a CLI interface","zh":"赋予代理生成使用asciinema的循环GIF的能力，提供完成任务的视觉证明，并通过演示和清理脚本实现快速审查，所有这些都通过CLI接口管理","ja":"asciinemaを使用してループGIFを生成するエージェントの能力を提供し、タスクの完了の視覚的な証拠を提供し、デモおよびクリーンアップスクリプトを使用して迅速なレビューを実現し、すべてをCLIインターフェイスで管理","ko":"에이전트가 asciinema를 사용하여 루핑 GIF를 생성할 수 있는 기능을 제공하여 작업 완료에 대한 시각적 증거를 제공하고 데모 및 클린업 스크립트를 통해 빠른 검토를 용이하게 하며 모든 것을 CLI 인터페이스를 통해 관리","es":"Habilita a los agentes a generar GIFs de bucle utilizando asciinema, proporcionando una prueba visual de tareas completadas y facilitando una revisión rápida con scripts de demostración y limpieza, todo gestionado a través de una interfaz de CLI","fr":"Permet aux agents de générer des GIFs de boucle à l''aide d''asciinema, fournissant une preuve visuelle de tâches achevées et facilitant une révision rapide avec des scripts de démonstration et de nettoyage, le tout géré via une interface CLI","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, mit asciinema GIFs in Schleife zu generieren, wodurch eine visuelle Bestätigung abgeschlossener Aufgaben bereitgestellt und eine schnelle Überprüfung mit Demo- und Bereinigungsskripten ermöglicht wird, die alle über eine CLI-Schnittstelle verwaltet werden","pt":"Habilita os agentes a gerar GIFs de loop usando asciinema, fornecendo prova visual de tarefas concluídas e facilitando a revisão rápida com scripts de demonstração e limpeza, todos gerenciados por meio de uma interface CLI","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью генерировать GIF-изображения с помощью asciinema, предоставляя визуальное подтверждение выполненных задач и облегчая быстрый обзор с помощью демонстрационных и очистных скриптов, все управляемые через интерфейс CLI","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على生成 GIFs متكررة باستخدام asciinema، مما يوفر دليلًا مرئيًا على المهام المكتملة ويسهل الاستعراض السريع مع 脚本 العرض والتنظيف، وكلها يتم إدارتها من خلال واجهة CLI"},"useCases":{"en":["Creating terminal demo recordings","Generating looping GIFs for task verification","Automating demo script creation"],"zh":["创建终端演示录像","生成任务验证的循环GIF","自动化演示脚本创建"],"ja":["ターミナルデモレコーディングの作成","タスク検証用のループGIFの生成","デモスクリプト作成の自動化"],"ko":["터미널 데모 녹화 생성","작업 확인을 위한 루핑 GIF 생성","데모 스크립트 생성 자동화"],"es":["Crear grabaciones de demostración de terminal","Generar GIFs de bucle para la verificación de tareas","Automatizar la creación de scripts de demostración"],"fr":["Créer des enregistrements de démonstration de terminal","Générer des GIFs de boucle pour la vérification de tâches","Automatiser la création de scripts de démonstration"],"de":["Terminal-Demo-Aufnahmen erstellen","GIFs in Schleife für die Aufgabenüberprüfung generieren","Demo-Skript-Erstellung automatisieren"],"pt":["Criação de gravações de demonstração de terminal","Geração de GIFs de loop para verificação de tarefas","Criação automática de scripts de demonstração"],"ru":["Создание записей демонстрации терминала","Генерация GIF-изображений для проверки задач","Автоматическое создание демонстрационных скриптов"],"ar":["إنشاء تسجيلات демонстрация لمحطة الطرفية","إنشاء GIFs متكررة لتحقق من المهام","إنشاء 脚本 العرض تلقائيًا"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires asciinema installation","Limited to terminal-based demonstrations","Recording length limited to 5-20 seconds"],"zh":["需要安装asciinema","仅限于基于终端的演示","录制长度限制在5-20秒"],"ja":["asciinemaのインストールが必要","ターミナルベースのデモに限定","レコーディングの長さが5〜20秒に制限"],"ko":["asciinema 설치가 필요","터미널 기반 데모로 제한","녹화 길이 제한 5-20초"],"es":["Requiere la instalación de asciinema","Limitado a demostraciones basadas en terminal","La duración de la grabación está limitada a 5-20 segundos"],"fr":["Nécessite l''installation d''asciinema","Limité aux démonstrations basées sur le terminal","La durée de l''enregistrement est limitée à 5-20 secondes"],"de":["Erfordert die Installation von asciinema","Begrenzt auf terminalbasierte Demonstrationen","Die Aufnahmedauer ist auf 5-20 Sekunden begrenzt"],"pt":["Requer instalação do asciinema","Limitado a demonstrações baseadas em terminal","Duração da gravação limitada a 5-20 segundos"],"ru":["Требуется установка asciinema","Ограничен демонстрациями на основе терминала","Длительность записи ограничена 5-20 секундами"],"ar":["يتطلب تركيب asciinema","محدود بالتظاهرات القائمة على المحطة الطرفية","مدة التسجيل محدودة ب 5-20 ثانية"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"9047933f79a5bab80985a589b1f0ecab9ec1267c4bc08dd949732d8e27ae1e05","qualityScore":40}');
