tung von Vorschlägen für Kommentare","Integration mit dem ToolHive-Ökosystem","KI-Tool für die Zusammenarbeit","Verbesserung der Effizienz im Kommentierungsprozess"],"pt":["Repositório central para submissão de RFCs","Colaboração entre desenvolvedores","Melhoria das ferramentas de IA","Integração com o ecossistema ToolHive","Suporte a desenvolvedores de ferramentas de IA"],"ru":["Центральный репозиторий для подачи RFC","Сотрудничество между разработчиками","Улучшение ИИ Агентов","Интеграция с экосистемой ToolHive","Поддержка разработчиков ИИ Агентов"],"ar":["مستودع مركزي لتقديم RFCs","التعاون بين المطورين","تحسين أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","التكامل مع نظام ToolHive","دعم مطوري أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي"]},"keywords":{"zh":["如何使用write-rfc","write-rfc教程","ToolHive生态系统RFC","write-rfc安装","write-rfc设置指南","write-rfc vs github","write-rfc替代方案","什么是write-rfc"],"ja":["write-rfcの使い方","write-rfcチュートリアル","ToolHiveエコシステムのRFC","write-rfcのインストール","write-rfcの設定ガイド","write-rfc vs github","write-rfcの代替","write-rfcとは"],"ko":["write-rfc 사용법","write-rfc 튜토리얼","ToolHive 생태계의 RFC","write-rfc 설치","write-rfc 설정 가이드","write-rfc vs github","write-rfc 대안","write-rfc란"],"es":["cómo usar write-rfc","qué es write-rfc","herramientas de AI para la colaboración","alternativas a write-rfc","write-rfc vs otras herramientas","instalación de write-rfc","guía de configuración de write-rfc"],"fr":["comment utiliser write-rfc","qu''est-ce que write-rfc","outils d''IA pour la collaboration","alternatives à write-rfc","write-rfc vs d''autres outils","installation de write-rfc","guide de configuration de write-rfc"],"de":["wie man write-rfc verwendet","was ist write-rfc","KI-Tools für die Zusammenarbeit","Alternativen zu write-rfc","write-rfc vs andere Tools","Installation von write-rfc","Konfigurationsanleitung für write-rfc"],"pt":["ferramentas de ia","write-rfc","ecossistema toolhive","como usar write-rfc","o que é write-rfc","alternativas ao write-rfc","write-rfc vs github","instalar write-rfc","guia de configuração do write-rfc"],"ru":["ИИ Агенты","write-rfc","экосистема toolhive","как использовать write-rfc","что такое write-rfc","альтернативы write-rfc","write-rfc vs github","установить write-rfc","руководство по настройке write-rfc"],"ar":["أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","write-rfc","نظام toolhive","كيفية استخدام write-rfc","ما هو write-rfc","بديلات write-rfc","write-rfc vs github","تثبيت write-rfc","دليل إعداد write-rfc"]}},"owner":"stacklok","repo":"toolhive-rfcs","repoPath":"stacklok/toolhive-rfcs","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-04T13:07:01.721Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"write-rfc","description":"Write RFCs for the ToolHive ecosystem. Use when the user wants to create a new RFC, proposal, or design document for toolhive, toolhive-studio, toolhive-registry, toolhive-registry-server, toolhive-cloud-ui, or dockyard projects.","bodyPreview":"# Write RFC Skill\n\nThis skill helps you write high-quality RFCs for the ToolHive ecosystem following established patterns and conventions.\n\n## Overview\n\nToolHive RFCs follow a specific format with the naming convention `THV-{NUMBER}-{descriptive-name}.md`. The NUMBER must match the PR number and be zero-padded to 4 digits.\n\n## Workflow\n\n### Step 1: Gather Requirements\n\nBefore writing an RFC, ask the user about:\n\n1. **Problem Statement**: What problem are they trying to solve?\n2. **Target Reposit","body":"# Write RFC Skill\n\nThis skill helps you write high-quality RFCs for the ToolHive ecosystem following established patterns and conventions.\n\n## Overview\n\nToolHive RFCs follow a specific format with the naming convention `THV-{NUMBER}-{descriptive-name}.md`. The NUMBER must match the PR number and be zero-padded to 4 digits.\n\n## Workflow\n\n### Step 1: Gather Requirements\n\nBefore writing an RFC, ask the user about:\n\n1. **Problem Statement**: What problem are they trying to solve?\n2. **Target Repository**: Which repo does this affect?\n   - `toolhive` - Core runtime, CLI (`thv`), operator (`thv-operator`), proxy-runner (`thv-proxyrunner`), virtual MCP (`vmcp`)\n   - `toolhive-studio` - Desktop UI application (Electron/TypeScript)\n   - `toolhive-registry` - MCP server registry data\n   - `toolhive-registry-server` - Registry API server (`thv-registry-api`)\n   - `toolhive-cloud-ui` - Cloud/Enterprise web UI (Next.js)\n   - `dockyard` - Container packaging for MCP servers\n   - `multiple` - Cross-cutting changes\n3. **Scope**: What are the goals and explicit non-goals?\n\n### Step 2: Research the Ecosystem\n\nBefore drafting, research the relevant codebase:\n\n#### 2.1 Fetch Architectural Documentation\n\nUse `mcp__github__get_file_contents` to read from `stacklok/toolhive` repo''s `docs/arch/` directory:\n\n| Document | Content |\n|----------|---------|\n| `00-overview.md` | Platform overview, key components |\n| `01-deployment-modes.md` | Local vs Kubernetes modes |\n| `02-core-concepts.md` | Nouns (Workloads, Transports, Proxy, etc.) and Verbs |\n| `03-transport-architecture.md` | stdio, SSE, streamable-http transports |\n| `04-secrets-management.md` | Secrets handling, providers |\n| `05-runconfig-and-permissions.md` | Configuration format, permission profiles |\n| `06-registry-system.md` | Registry architecture, MCPRegistry CRD |\n| `07-groups.md` | Server grouping concepts |\n| `08-workloads-lifecycle.md` | Lifecycle management |\n| `09-operator-architecture.md` | K8s operator, CRDs |\n| `10-virtual-mcp-architecture.md` | Virtual MCP aggregation |\n\n#### 2.2 Review Existing RFCs\n\nRead `rfcs/` directory in this repository to understand patterns and check for related proposals.\n\n#### 2.3 Search Relevant Codebases\n\nUse `mcp__github__search_code` or `mcp__github__get_file_contents` to explore:\n\n| Repository | Purpose |\n|------------|---------|\n| `stacklok/toolhive` | Core platform, CLI, operator, proxy |\n| `stacklok/toolhive-studio` | Desktop UI |\n| `stacklok/toolhive-registry-server` | Registry API server |\n| `stacklok/toolhive-registry` | Registry data |\n| `stacklok/toolhive-cloud-ui` | Cloud/Enterprise UI |\n| `stacklok/dockyard` | Container packaging |\n\n### Step 3: Draft the RFC\n\nCreate the RFC following the template structure from `rfcs/0000-template.md`.\n\n#### Required Metadata\n\n```markdown\n# RFC-XXXX: Title\n\n- **Status**: Draft\n- **Author(s)**: Name (@github-handle)\n- **Created**: YYYY-MM-DD\n- **Last Updated**: YYYY-MM-DD\n- **Target Repository**: [from step 1]\n- **Related Issues**: [links if applicable]\n```\n\n#### Core Sections\n\n1. **Summary** - 2-3 sentences capturing the essence\n2. **Problem Statement** - Current limitation, who''s affected, why it matters\n3. **Goals** - Specific objectives (bulleted)\n4. **Non-Goals** - Explicit scope boundaries\n5. **Proposed Solution**\n   - High-Level Design (with Mermaid diagrams)\n   - Detailed Design: Component changes, API changes, configuration changes, data model changes\n6. **Security Considerations** (REQUIRED) - See security checklist below\n7. **Alternatives Considered** - Other approaches evaluated\n8. **Compatibility** - Backward and forward compatibility\n9. **Implementation Plan** - Phased approach with tasks\n10. **Testing Strategy** - Unit, integration, E2E, performance, security tests\n11. **Documentation** - What needs documenting\n12. **Open Questions** - Unresolved items\n13. **References** - Related links\n\n#### Security Considerations Checklist (REQUIRED)\n\nEvery RFC MUST address:\n\n- [ ] **Threat Model** - Potential threats, attacker capabilities\n- [ ] **Authentication and Authorization** - Auth changes, permission models\n- [ ] **Data Security** - Sensitive data handling, encryption\n- [ ] **Input Validation** - User input, injection vectors\n- [ ] **Secrets Management** - Credentials storage, rotation\n- [ ] **Audit and Logging** - Security events, compliance\n- [ ] **Mitigations** - Security controls implemented\n\n### Step 4: Use Proper Conventions\n\n#### Code Examples\n\n- Use **Go** for API changes in toolhive, toolhive-registry-server\n- Use **TypeScript** for toolhive-studio, toolhive-cloud-ui changes\n- Use **YAML** for configuration examples\n- Use **Mermaid** for diagrams (flowcharts, sequence diagrams)\n\n#### Kubernetes CRDs\n\nIf the RFC involves Kubernetes, include CRD examples:\n\n```yaml\napiVersion: toolhive.stacklok.dev/v1alpha1\nkind: MCPServer\nmetadata:\n  name: example\nspec:\n  # ...\n```\n\nCRD types: `MCPServer`, `MCPRegistry`, `MCPToolConfig`, `MCPExternalAuthConfig`, `MCPGroup`, `VirtualMCPServer`\n\n### Step 5: File Naming\n\nThe RFC file should be named `THV-XXXX-{descriptive-name}.md` where XXXX is the PR number. Since you don''t know the PR number yet, use a placeholder like `THV-XXXX-{name}.md` and remind the user to rename it to match the PR number after creating the PR.\n\n### Step 6: Review Checklist\n\nBefore finalizing, verify:\n\n- [ ] Problem is clearly stated\n- [ ] Goals and non-goals are explicit\n- [ ] Security section is complete (all 7 areas addressed)\n- [ ] Alternatives are discussed\n- [ ] Diagrams illustrate complex flows\n- [ ] Code examples are concrete and in the correct language\n- [ ] Implementation phases are defined\n- [ ] Testing strategy covers all levels\n- [ ] File follows naming convention\n\n## ToolHive Architecture Summary\n\n### Platform Overview\n\nToolHive is a **platform** for MCP server management (not just a container runner):\n\n- **Proxy layer** with middleware (auth, authz, audit, rate limiting)\n- **Security** by default (network isolation, permission profiles)\n- **Aggregation** via Virtual MCP Server\n- **Registry** for curated MCP servers\n- **Multi-deployment**: Local (CLI/UI) and Kubernetes (operator)\n\n### Key Binaries\n\n| Binary | Location | Purpose |\n|--------|----------|---------|\n| `thv` | toolhive | Main CLI |\n| `thv-operator` | toolhive | Kubernetes operator |\n| `thv-proxyrunner` | toolhive | K8s proxy container |\n| `vmcp` | toolhive | Virtual MCP server (aggregation) |\n| `thv-registry-api` | toolhive-registry-server | Registry API server |\n\n### Transport Types\n\n- **stdio** - Standard input/output (requires protocol translation)\n- **SSE** - Server-Sent Events (HTTP, transparent proxy)\n- **streamable-http** - HTTP streaming (transparent proxy)\n\n### Design Principles\n\n1. Platform abstraction over direct execution\n2. Security by default (network isolation, permissions)\n3. Extensibility through middleware\n4. Cloud-native (K8s operators, containers)\n5. RunConfig as portable API contract\n\n## Reference Files\n\n- Template: `rfcs/0000-template.md`\n- Contributing guide: `CONTRIBUTING.md`\n- Existing RFCs: `rfcs/THV-*.md`\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-04T13:51:46.159Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for AI Agents needing structured proposal drafting for the ToolHive ecosystem","zh":"非常适合需要为 ToolHive 生态系统编写结构化提案的 AI Agents","ja":"ToolHive エコシステムの構造化提案作成を必要とする AI エージェントに最適","ko":"ToolHive 생태계를 위한 구조화된 제안서 초안 작성이 필요한 AI 에이전트에 적합","es":"Perfecto para agentes de IA que necesitan redactar propuestas estructuradas para el ecosistema ToolHive","fr":"Parfait pour les agents IA qui ont besoin de rédiger des propositions structurées pour l''écosystème ToolHive","de":"Perfekt für KI-Agents, die strukturierte Vorschläge für das ToolHive-Ökosystem benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de IA que necessitam de redação de propostas estruturadas para o ecossistema ToolHive","ru":"Идеально для ИИ-агентов, которым требуется структурированное составление предложений для экосистемы ToolHive","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الذكية التي تحتاج إلى صياغة مقترحات منظمات للنظام البيئي ToolHive"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to generate high-quality RFCs following established patterns and conventions, utilizing markdown files with specific naming conventions like THV-{NUMBER}-{descriptive-name}.md, and adhering to zero-padded 4-digit numbering","zh":"赋予代理生成高质量的 RFC，遵循既定的模式和约定，利用具有特定命名约定的 markdown 文件，如 THV-{NUMBER}-{descriptive-name}.md，并遵循零填充的 4 位数字编号","ja":"エージェントが既存のパターンと規約に従って高品質の RFC を生成することを可能にし、特定の命名規約 (THV-{NUMBER}-{descriptive-name}.md) の markdown ファイルを利用し、0 パディングの 4 桁の番号付けに従う","ko":"에이전트가既存의 패턴과 규약을 따르는 높은 품질의 RFC를 생성할 수 있도록 하며, 특정 명명 규칙(THV-{NUMBER}-{descriptive-name}.md)을 갖는 markdown 파일을 사용하며, 0 패딩 4자리 번호 지정에 따라야 함","es":"Habilita a los agentes a generar RFC de alta calidad siguiendo patrones y convenciones establecidos, utilizando archivos markdown con convenciones de nomenclatura específicas como THV-{NUMBER}-{descriptive-name}.md, y ajustándose a un número de cuatro dígitos con relleno de ceros","fr":"Permet aux agents de générer des RFC de haute qualité en suivant des modèles et des conventions établis, en utilisant des fichiers markdown avec des conventions de nommage spécifiques comme THV-{NUMBER}-{descriptive-name}.md, et en respectant un numérotage à quatre chiffres avec padding zéro","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agenten, RFCs in hoher Qualität zu generieren, indem sie etablierte Muster und Konventionen befolgen, mittels markdown-Dateien mit spezifischen Benennungskonventionen wie THV-{NUMBER}-{descriptive-name}.md, und sich an eine Null-Padding-4-Stellen-Nummerierung anpassen","pt":"Habilita agentes a gerar RFCs de alta qualidade seguindo padrões e convenções estabelecidas, utilizando arquivos markdown com convenções de nomenclatura específicas como THV-{NUMBER}-{descriptive-name}.md, e aderindo a numeração com zeros à esquerda de 4 dígitos","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью генерировать высококачественные RFC, следуя установленным шаблонам и соглашениям, используя файлы markdown с конкретными соглашениями об именовании, такими как THV-{NUMBER}-{descriptive-name}.md, и придерживаясь нумерации с четырьмя знаками и заполнением нулями","ar":"تمكين الوكلاء من توليدRFCs عالية الجودة اتباعا للأنماط والمواصفات المحددة، باستخدام ملفات markdown مع اتفاقيات تسمية محددة مثل THV-{NUMBER}-{descriptive-name}.md، والالتزام بالترقيم بأربعة أرقام ومملوءة بالاصفار"},"useCases":{"en":["Automating RFC template generation","Standardizing problem statement descriptions","Streamlining target repository identification"],"zh":["自动化 RFC 模板生成","标准化问题描述","简化目标仓库识别"],"ja":["RFC テンプレートの自動生成","問題文書の標準化","ターゲットリポジトリの識別の簡素化"],"ko":["RFC 템플릿 자동 생성","문제 설명의 표준화","대상 저장소 식별의 간소화"],"es":["Automatización de la generación de plantillas de RFC","Establecimiento de descripciones de declaraciones de problemas estandarizadas","Optimización de la identificación del repositorio objetivo"],"fr":["Automatisation de la génération de modèles de RFC","Standardisation des descriptions de déclarations de problèmes","Optimisation de l''identification du référentiel cible"],"de":["Automatisierung der Erstellung von RFC-Vorlagen","Standardisierung von Problembeschreibungen","Optimierung der Identifizierung des Ziel-Repositorys"],"pt":["Automatizar geração de modelos de RFC","Padronizar descrições de declarações de problemas","Otimizar identificação de repositórios de destino"],"ru":["Автоматизировать генерацию шаблонов RFC","Стандартизировать описания заявлений о проблемах","Оптимизировать определение целевых репозиториев"],"ar":["آليّة توليد قوالب RFC","تقييس وصفات بيان المشكلات","تحسين تحديد مخازن المستهدفة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires knowledge of ToolHive ecosystem conventions","Limited to markdown file format","Needs user input for problem statement and target repository"],"zh":["需要了解 ToolHive 生态系统的约定","仅限 markdown 文件格式","需要用户输入问题描述和目标仓库"],"ja":["ToolHive エコシステムの規約の知識が必要","markdown ファイル形式のみ","問題文書とターゲットリポジトリのユーザー入力が必要"],"ko":["ToolHive 생태계의 규약을了解해야 함","markdown 파일 형식만 해당","문제 설명과 대상 저장소에 대한 사용자 입력이 필요"],"es":["Requiere conocimiento de las convenciones del ecosistema ToolHive","Limitado al formato de archivo markdown","Necesita la entrada del usuario para la declaración del problema y el repositorio objetivo"],"fr":["Nécessite une connaissance des conventions de l''écosystème ToolHive","Limité au format de fichier markdown","Nécessite une entrée utilisateur pour la déclaration du problème et le référentiel cible"],"de":["Benötigt Kenntnisse der Konventionen des ToolHive-Ökosystems","Begrenzt auf das markdown-Dateiformat","Benötigt Benutzereingaben für die Problembeschreibung und das Ziel-Repository"],"pt":["Requer conhecimento das convenções do ecossistema ToolHive","Limitado ao formato de arquivo markdown","Necessita de entrada do usuário para declaração de problemas e repositório de destino"],"ru":["Требует знания соглашений экосистемы ToolHive","Ограничен форматом файла markdown","Требует ввода пользователя для заявления о проблемах и целевого репозитория"],"ar":["يتطلب معرفة الاتفاقيات لنظام بيئي ToolHive","محدود بتنسيق ملف markdown","يحتاج إلى إدخال المستخدم لبيان المشكلة ومستودع المستهدفة"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"2f7c52bbc5f05bc117c14892aa05ad235ff55ea37bc7d842ab1b4fa0375c419f","qualityScore":40}');
