,"Suporte a CLI para automação de tarefas"],"ru":["Создание приложений в реальном времени","Создание и обмен приложениями","Скачивание персонализированных приложений","Интеграция с технологиями seperti React и Node.js","Поддержка CLI для автоматизации задач"],"ar":["تطوير التطبيقات في الوقت الفعلي","إنشاء وتشارك التطبيقات","تنزيل التطبيقات المخصصة","التكامل مع تقنيات مثل React و Node.js","دعم CLI للautomatisation المهام"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI智能代理","ui工具","实时演化应用","共享应用开发","如何使用AI智能代理","AI智能代理安装","AI智能代理设置指南"],"ja":["AIエージェント","ui機能","アプリの共同開発","進化的なアプリ開発","AIエージェントの使い方","AIエージェントのインストール","AIエージェントの設定ガイド"],"ko":["AI 에이전트","ui 툴","애플리케이션 공동 개발","진화적인 애플리케이션 개발","AI 에이전트 사용법","AI 에이전트 설치","AI 에이전트 설정 가이드"],"es":["cómo usar herramientas de UI","qué es un agente de IA","alternativas a herramientas de UI","herramientas de UI vs competidores","instalar herramientas de UI","guía de configuración de herramientas de UI","desarrollo de aplicaciones con Agentes de IA","herramientas de UI para desarrolladores"],"fr":["comment utiliser des outils d''UI","qu''est-ce qu''un agent d''IA","alternatives aux outils d''UI","outils d''UI vs concurrents","installer des outils d''UI","guide de configuration des outils d''UI","développement d''applications avec des Agents d''IA","outils d''UI pour développeurs"],"de":["wie man UI-Tools verwendet","was ist ein KI-Agent","Alternativen zu UI-Tools","UI-Tools vs Wettbewerber","Installation von UI-Tools","Konfigurationsanleitung für UI-Tools","Entwicklung von Anwendungen mit KI-Agents","UI-Tools für Entwickler"],"pt":["como usar agente de IA para UI","o que é agente de IA para UI","alternativas para agente de IA para UI","agente de IA para UI vs outros","instalar agente de IA para UI","guia de configuração do agente de IA para UI"],"ru":["как использовать ИИ Агент для UI","что такое ИИ Агент для UI","альтернативы для ИИ Агента для UI","ИИ Агент для UI vs другие","установить ИИ Агент для UI","руководство по настройке ИИ Агента для UI"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام وكيل الذكاء الاصطناعي لواجهة المستخدم","ما هو وكيل الذكاء الاصطناعي لواجهة المستخدم","بديلات لوكيل الذكاء الاصطناعي لواجهة المستخدم","وكيل الذكاء الاصطناعي لواجهة المستخدم مقابل الآخرين","تثبيت وكيل الذكاء الاصطناعي لواجهة المستخدم","دليل إعداد وكيل الذكاء الاصطناعي لواجهة المستخدم"]}},"owner":"zot","repo":"frictionless","repoPath":"zot/frictionless","stars":4,"forks":2,"updatedAt":"2026-02-25T22:58:57Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"ui","description":"use when **running Frictionless UIs** or needing to understand UI structure (before modifying one)","bodyPreview":"# UI MCP\n\nFoundation for building and running ui-engine UIs with Lua apps connected to widgets.\n\n## Simple Requests\n\nWhen the user says `/ui`, show app-console as in Quick Start. Prefer Playwright if the user has been using it.\n\nWhen the user says `show APP`, show APP as in Quick Start. Prefer Playwright if the user has been using it.\n\nWhen the user says `events` it means to start the event loop, but not use `.ui/mcp display` or `.ui/mcp browser` as in Quick Start.\n\n## Helper Script Reference\n\nT","body":"# UI MCP\n\nFoundation for building and running ui-engine UIs with Lua apps connected to widgets.\n\n## Simple Requests\n\nWhen the user says `/ui`, show app-console as in Quick Start. Prefer Playwright if the user has been using it.\n\nWhen the user says `show APP`, show APP as in Quick Start. Prefer Playwright if the user has been using it.\n\nWhen the user says `events` it means to start the event loop, but not use `.ui/mcp display` or `.ui/mcp browser` as in Quick Start.\n\n## Helper Script Reference\n\nThe `.ui/mcp` script provides commands for interacting with the UI server. **Always use relative paths** (never absolute — absolute paths break the user''s permission rules).\n\n**`{url}` means the UI server URL** — read the port from `.ui/ui-port` and construct `http://localhost:{port}`. This is NOT the MCP connection port — it''s the UI''s own HTTP server. Use `.ui/mcp status` when you also need session count or base_dir.\n\n**CRITICAL: URLs must NEVER include session IDs.** Always use `{url}/?conserve=true` (root URL). Session IDs in URLs will cause problems.\n\n| Command | Description |\n|---------|-------------|\n| `.ui/mcp status` | Get server status (url, sessions, base_dir) |\n| `.ui/mcp browser` | Open browser to `{url}/?conserve=true` |\n| `.ui/mcp display APP` | Display APP in the browser |\n| `.ui/mcp run ''lua code''` | Execute Lua code in session |\n| `.ui/mcp event` | Wait for next UI event (120s timeout) |\n| `.ui/mcp state` | Get current session state |\n| `.ui/mcp variables` | Get current variable values |\n| `.ui/mcp audit APP` | Run code quality audit on APP |\n| `.ui/mcp progress APP PERCENT STAGE` | Report build progress |\n| `.ui/mcp linkapp add\\|remove APP` | Manage app symlinks |\n| `.ui/mcp checkpoint CMD APP [MSG]` | Manage checkpoints (save/list/rollback/diff/clear) |\n| `.ui/mcp theme list` | List available themes |\n| `.ui/mcp theme classes [THEME]` | List semantic classes for theme |\n| `.ui/mcp theme audit APP [THEME]` | Audit app''s theme class usage |\n\n## Quick Start: Show an Existing App\n\n### A. Read the design\n\nRead `{base_dir}/apps/APP/design.md` to learn the global variable name (e.g., `claudePanel`) and event types.\n\n### B. Display the app\n\n- Use `.ui/mcp run` to check if `mcp.value.type == AppName` (PascalCase version of app-name)\n  - If not, use `.ui/mcp display app-name`\n- If Playwright is connected:\n  - `browser_evaluate` with `function: \"() => window.location.href\"` to get current URL\n  - If URL does NOT start with `{url}/`, then `browser_navigate` to `{url}/mark-playwright.html?url={url}/?conserve=true`\n  - **ONLY use mark-playwright.html when navigating via Playwright.** Never use it for `.ui/mcp browser`.\n  - Do not wait for page to display or take a snapshot\n- Otherwise, run `.ui/mcp browser`\n\n### C. Start the event loop\n\n```\nBash(.ui/mcp event, run_in_background=true)\n```\n\nThe UI will NOT respond to clicks until this is running.\n\n### D. Handle events\n\n- Parse JSON: `[{\"app\":\"app-console\",\"event\":\"select\",\"name\":\"contacts\"}]`\n- Read design.md''s \"Events\" section for how to handle each event type\n- **For UI changes**: Check event''s `handler` field and invoke that skill\n- Simple state changes: use `.ui/mcp run` directly\n- Kill old task, then restart: `Bash(.ui/mcp event, run_in_background=true)`\n\n---\n\n## Details\n\n### Step A: The `app` field\n\n**The `app` field is the ONLY field that determines which design.md you read.** Do NOT be misled by `context`, `note`, `name`, or other fields that mention other app names — these are event data, not the source app.\n\n```\nEvent: {\"app\":\"app-console\", \"event\":\"app_created\", \"name\":\"contacts\", \"context\":\"contacts\"}\n       ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\nRead:  .ui/apps/app-console/design.md  <-- ONLY use the \"app\" field\n```\n\nDo NOT skip reading design.md — even for events that seem obvious like `app_created`.\n\n### Step C: Event loop lifecycle\n\n**Only ONE listener may exist at a time** — the script enforces this via `.ui/.eventpid` and will error if a listener is already running.\n\n**Task lifecycle:**\n1. Run `.ui/mcp event` with `Bash(run_in_background=true)`, save the task_id. If it errors with \"already running\", do nothing — the script manages the PID lock itself. Do NOT manually check PIDs or the `.eventpid` file; just wait for the existing listener to complete.\n2. When the background task completes, **ALWAYS read the output file immediately** — do NOT assume timeout. Failing to read means silently dropping events.\n3. Handle any events received\n4. Start a fresh listener (go to step 1)\n\n**Exit codes:**\n- 0 + JSON output = events received (may be empty array `[]` for timeout)\n- 52 = server restarted (restart both server and event loop)\n\n**After `ui_configure`:** Restart the event loop — reconfiguring changes the MCP port that `.ui/mcp event` uses.\n\n### Step D: Handler dispatch and build settings\n\n**NEVER modify or create UI code directly.** When an event requires UI changes, check the `handler` field and invoke that skill. This applies to ALL UI modifications — requirements, design, code, and viewdefs.\n\nEvery event has two fields injected automatically based on the status bar toggles:\n\n| Toggle | Field | Values |\n|--------|-------|--------|\n| Build mode (rocket/diamond) | `handler` | `\"/ui-fast\"` or `\"/ui-thorough\"` |\n| Execution (hourglass/arrows) | `background` | `false` or `true` |\n\nThese reflect the user''s explicit choices. For background execution:\n```\nTask(subagent_type=\"ui-builder\", run_in_background=true, prompt=\"invoke {handler} skill...\")\n```\n\n---\n\n## App Variable Convention\n\nEach app defines a **global variable** for interacting with it via `.ui/mcp run`:\n\n| App Name       | Global Variable | Example Call                        |\n|----------------|-----------------|-------------------------------------|\n| `claude-panel` | `claudePanel`   | `claudePanel:addAgentMessage(\"Hi\")` |\n| `contacts`     | `contacts`      | `contacts:addContact(name, email)`  |\n| `ma-luba`      | `maLuba`        | `maLuba:someMethod()`               |\n\n**Convention:** kebab-case app name → camelCase variable. The global variable is exactly the camelCase conversion of the app directory name (no \"App\" suffix).\n\nFind the variable by looking at the bottom of `app.lua` for the instance creation:\n```lua\nif not session.reloading then\n    claudePanel = ClaudePanel:new()  -- <-- this is the global variable\nend\n```\n\n## Chat Messages\n\nAll chat messages render markdown. Use it via `.ui/mcp run`:\n```\n.ui/mcp run ''mcp:addAgentMessage(\"Found **salary data**: $150k-$180k\")''\n```\n\n### Pointing at UI elements\n\nWhen the user asks \"where is X?\" or \"show me the Y\", **both highlight the element AND include a clickable link** in your response so the user can re-trigger the highlight later:\n\n1. Find the element''s DOM id (from variables, viewdefs, or Playwright)\n2. Highlight it immediately: `mcp.code = [=[window.uiApp.highlight(\"ui-42\")// ]=] .. os.time()`\n3. Reply with a rich message containing a highlight link:\n\n```lua\nmcp:addRichMessage(\n    \"The search box is \"\n    .. mcp:highlightLink(\"ui-42\", \"right here\")\n    .. \". Type to filter the list.\"\n)\n```\n\nThe link stays in the chat history — the user can click it anytime to re-highlight the element.\n\n### Message methods\n\n| Method | Description |\n|--------|-------------|\n| `mcp:addAgentMessage(text)` | Agent message with markdown rendering |\n| `mcp:addRichMessage(html)` | Agent message with raw HTML (for highlight links, custom content) |\n| `mcp:highlightLink(elementId, label)` | Returns anchor HTML that highlights an element on click |\n| `mcp:addAgentThinking(text)` | Thinking/progress message (italic, updates status bar) |\n| `mcp:renderMarkdown(text)` | Convert markdown to HTML fragment (for custom use) |\n\n## Building or Modifying UIs\n\nWhen the user asks for changes outside an event loop, ask which mode they prefer or default to `/ui-fast` for small changes.\n\n**Before building a new app:**\n1. Create the app directory: `mkdir -p {base_dir}/apps/<app>`\n2. Write requirements to `{base_dir}/apps/<app>/requirements.md`\n\n### Requirements Format\n\n```markdown\n# Descriptive Title\n\nA short paragraph describing what the app does.\n\n## Section 1\n...\n```\n\nThe first line is a descriptive title (e.g., \"# Contact Manager\"), followed by prose describing the app. See `.claude/skills/ui-builder/examples/requirements.md` for a reference.\n\n## Directory Structure\n\n```\n{base_dir}/\n├── apps/<app>/           # App source files\n│   ├── requirements.md   # What to build (you write this)\n│   ├── design.md         # How it works (generated)\n│   ├── app.lua           # Lua code (generated)\n│   └── viewdefs/         # HTML templates (generated)\n├── lua/                  # Symlinks to app lua files\n├── viewdefs/             # Symlinks to app viewdefs\n├── html/<app>            # Symlink to app dir (serves static files at /<app>/)\n├── html/<app>-storage    # Symlink to storage dir (serves at /<app>-storage/)\n├── storage/<app>/        # Optional local storage (isolated from app updates)\n├── patterns/             # Reusable pattern documentation\n├── themes/               # Theme definitions and CSS variables\n├── event                 # Event wait script\n└── log/                  # Runtime logs\n```\n\n## File Ownership\n\n- `requirements.md` — you write/update this\n- `design.md`, `app.lua`, `viewdefs/` — **MUST load `/ui-basics` first**, then use `/ui-fast` or `/ui-thorough`. This is a non-standard system; standard web patterns will lead you astray.\n\n## Debugging\n\n- **Lua logs:** `{base_dir}/log/lua.log` for Lua errors\n- **MCP server stderr:** `.ui/log/mcp.log`\n- **Variable inspector:** `http://localhost:{mcp-port}/variables` (read port from `.ui/mcp-port`) — curl for JSON, browser for interactive inspector\n- **MCP resources:** `ui://variables` (full variable tree), `ui://state` (live state JSON)\n- **JS diagnostics:** `window.uiApp.getStore()` (variable state) and `window.uiApp.getBinding()` (widget bindings) in browser console\n- **Remote JS execution:** Set `mcp.code` from Lua — bound to `ui-code` in the MCP shell, enabling JS execution in the browser. Critical when using a system browser instead of Playwright. Re-assigning the same value is a no-op (change detection); append a nonce to re-execute (e.g., `code .. \"\\n// \" .. nonce`)\n- `.ui/mcp run` returns error messages\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-26T08:38:40.998Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for AI Agents needing interactive user interface capabilities with Lua apps and widgets.","zh":"非常适合需要与Lua应用和小部件交互的用户界面功能的AI代理。","ja":"Luaアプリとウィジェットとのインタラクティブなユーザーインターフェイス機能を必要とするAIエージェントに最適です。","ko":"Lua 애플리케이션 및 위젯과 상호 작용할 수 있는 대화형 사용자 인터페이스 기능이 필요한 AI 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de IA que necesitan capacidades de interfaz de usuario interactiva con aplicaciones y widgets Lua.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents IA nécessitant des capacités d''interface utilisateur interactive avec des applications et des widgets Lua.","de":"Perfekt für KI-Agents, die interaktive Benutzeroberflächenfunktionen mit Lua-Apps und -Widgets benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de IA que necessitam de capacidades de interface do usuário interativa com aplicativos e widgets Lua.","ru":"Идеально для агентов ИИ, которым необходимы возможности интерактивного пользовательского интерфейса с приложениями и виджетами Lua.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي الذين يحتاجون إلى قدرات واجهة المستخدم التفاعلية مع تطبيقات Lua والwidgets."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to build and run ui-engine UIs with connected widgets, utilizing Lua apps and protocols like Playwright, and enables event loop management with specific commands like `/ui` and `events`.","zh":"赋予代理构建和运行ui-engine UI，并连接小部件，利用Lua应用和Playwright等协议，并使用特定命令（如 `/ui` 和 `events`）启用事件循环管理。","ja":"エージェントがui-engine UIを構築して実行し、ウィジェットを接続してLuaアプリとPlaywrightなどのプロトコルを利用し、 `/ui`および`events`などの特定のコマンドを使用してイベントループ管理を可能にします。","ko":"에이전트가 ui-engine UI를 구축하고 실행하고 위젯을 연결하여 Lua 애플리케이션 및 Playwright와 같은 프로토콜을 사용하며, `/ui` 및 `events`와 같은 특정 명령을 사용하여 이벤트 루프 관리를 활성화합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear y ejecutar interfaces de usuario ui-engine con widgets conectados, utilizando aplicaciones Lua y protocolos como Playwright, y permite la gestión del bucle de eventos con comandos específicos como `/ui` y `events`.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer et d''exécuter des interfaces utilisateur ui-engine avec des widgets connectés, en utilisant des applications Lua et des protocoles comme Playwright, et permet la gestion de la boucle d''événements avec des commandes spécifiques comme `/ui` et `events`.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agents, ui-engine-Benutzeroberflächen mit verbundenen Widgets zu erstellen und auszuführen, indem Lua-Apps und Protokolle wie Playwright verwendet werden, und ermöglicht die Verwaltung der Ereignisschleife mit bestimmten Befehlen wie `/ui` und `events`.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a construir e executar UIs do ui-engine com widgets conectados, utilizando aplicativos Lua e protocolos como o Playwright, e permite o gerenciamento de loop de eventos com comandos específicos como `/ui` e `events`.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать и запускать UI-интерфейсы ui-engine с подключенными виджетами, используя приложения Lua и протоколы, такие как Playwright, и позволяет управлять циклом событий с помощью конкретных команд, таких как `/ui` и `events`.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من بناء وتشغيل واجهات ui-engine UI مع widgets متصلة، باستخدام تطبيقات Lua وبروتوكولات مثل Playwright، وتمكن من إدارة حلقة الأحداث بأوامر محددة مثل `/ui` و `events`."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating UI interactions with Playwright","Generating custom UI components with Lua","Debugging UI events with the event loop"],"zh":["使用Playwright自动化UI交互","使用Lua生成自定义UI组件","使用事件循环调试UI事件"],"ja":["Playwrightを使用したUIインタラクションの自動化","Luaを使用したカスタムUIコンポーネントの生成","イベントループを使用したUIイベントのデバッグ"],"ko":["Playwright를 사용한 UI 상호 작용 자동화","Lua를 사용한 사용자 정의 UI 구성 요소 생성","이벤트 루프를 사용한 UI 이벤트 디버깅"],"es":["Automatizar interacciones de interfaz de usuario con Playwright","Generar componentes de interfaz de usuario personalizados con Lua","Depurar eventos de interfaz de usuario con la bucle de eventos"],"fr":["Automatiser les interactions d''interface utilisateur avec Playwright","Générer des composants d''interface utilisateur personnalisés avec Lua","Déboguer les événements d''interface utilisateur avec la boucle d''événements"],"de":["Automatisieren von Benutzeroberflächeninteraktionen mit Playwright","Erstellen von benutzerdefinierten Benutzeroberflächenkomponenten mit Lua","Debuggen von Benutzeroberflächenereignissen mit der Ereignisschleife"],"pt":["Automatizar interações de UI com o Playwright","Gerar componentes personalizados de UI com Lua","Depurar eventos de UI com o loop de eventos"],"ru":["Автоматизировать взаимодействия с UI с помощью Playwright","Генерировать пользовательские компоненты UI с помощью Lua","Отлаживать события UI с помощью цикла событий"],"ar":["أتمتة تفاعلات واجهة المستخدم مع Playwright","_generating مكونات واجهة المستخدم المخصصة مع Lua","تصحيح أخطاء أحداث واجهة المستخدم مع حلقة الأحداث"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Lua support","Playwright preference may affect compatibility","Specific commands like `/ui` and `events` must be used"],"zh":["需要Lua支持","Playwright首选项可能会影响兼容性","必须使用特定命令（如 `/ui` 和 `events`）"],"ja":["Luaサポートが必要","Playwrightの優先順位によって互換性が影響を受ける可能性がある"," `/ui`および`events`などの特定のコマンドを使用する必要がある"],"ko":["Lua 지원이 필요함","Playwright 우선 순위가 호환성을 영향을 줄 수 있음","특정 명령 (`/ui` 및 `events` 등)이 반드시 사용되어야 함"],"es":["Requiere soporte para Lua","La preferencia de Playwright puede afectar la compatibilidad","Deben utilizarse comandos específicos como `/ui` y `events`"],"fr":["Nécessite un support pour Lua","La préférence pour Playwright peut affecter la compatibilité","Des commandes spécifiques comme `/ui` et `events` doivent être utilisées"],"de":["Benötigt Lua-Unterstützung","Die Präferenz für Playwright kann die Kompatibilität beeinflussen","Bestimmte Befehle wie `/ui` und `events` müssen verwendet werden"],"pt":["Requer suporte a Lua","Preferência do Playwright pode afetar a compatibilidade","Comandos específicos como `/ui` e `events` devem ser usados"],"ru":["Требуется поддержка Lua","Предпочтение Playwright может повлиять на совместимость","Конкретные команды, такие как `/ui` и `events`, должны быть использованы"],"ar":["يتطلب دعم Lua","يمكن أن يؤثر تفضيل Playwright على التوافق","يجب استخدام أوامر محددة مثل `/ui` و `events`"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"182b0049834589f72bb98ddf4554c3b351885fe9361de0471ac92c67f5d8e6a2","qualityScore":39}');
